+
+# Story RC3.7: Fraud-Signals Module
+
+**Status:** review
+**Epic:** RC3 (the referee collection funnel). Closes RC3. Depends on rc3-1…rc3-6 (merged; #602 was the last).
+**Model:** `zai-coding-cn/glm-5.2` (kimi quota down this cycle; glm-5.2 proven capable across rc3-2…rc3-6).
+**Perkins:** ON (fraud/privacy code + the AD-10 honesty invariant — the load-bearing rule). Round runs on glm-5.2 fallback while kimi is down.
+**GitHub issue:** #548
+
+## Story
+
+> As a landlord,
+> I want honest fraud signals on each reference,
+> So that I have clues about provenance — never fabricated detections, never verdicts.
+
+rc3-1…rc3-6 shipped the collection funnel: the SMS client + Twilio Lookup infra (rc3-1), templates + send helpers (rc3-2), the referee form session (rc3-3), the exit routes incl. the stop-link objection route (rc3-4), the cadence sweep (rc3-5), and the verified delivery webhooks (rc3-6). rc3-7 **closes RC3** by building the honest fraud-signals table (AD-10) — the clues-about-provenance layer that RC4's landlord panel will DISPLAY. rc3-7 computes + persists; RC4 renders.
+
+**The load-bearing rule (AD-10 honesty):** signals are clues about provenance — **never fabricated detections, never verdicts**. They never auto-reject or alter a score (§9.4). The v2-reserved signals emit `unknown` / `null` / **absent** rather than placeholders. Innocent reuse (a letting agent legitimately appearing across several applications) is NOT fraud.
+
+## The AD-10 signal table (the spine — exactly this, nothing more)
+
+| Signal | v1 mechanism | Collectible? | Honest v1 value |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `contact_reused_within_application` | Pure DB: same phone/email in two ref slots of one application | Yes | `true`/`false` |
+| `contact_duplicate_of_applicant` | Pure DB: referee contact == applicant's own (`application.email`/`phone`) | Yes | `true`/`false` |
+| `contact_reused_across_applications` | Pure DB: same contact under a **different** referee name across applications | Yes | `true`/`false` |
+| `line_type` | Twilio Lookup Line-Type (`lookup.lookup_line_type`) | Yes (keys optional) | `"mobile"`/`"landline"`/`"voip"`/`"unknown"` |
+| `voip_or_burner` | `lookup.voip(line_type)` — **honestly `voip` only**; "burner" is not detectable v1 | Yes | `true`/`false` |
+| `form_session.completion_seconds` | Server wall-clock `form_opened_at` → `submitted_at` (seconds) | Yes | int / `null` (no form yet) |
+| `form_session.ip_matches_applicant` | Referee form IP vs `application.submitted_ip_text` | Yes | `true`/`false`/`null` |
+| `form_session.device_fingerprint_match` | Referee UA vs `application.submitted_user_agent` — **NOT a JS fingerprint lib; labelled weak** | Yes, weak | `true`/`false`/`null` |
+| `form_session.focus_seconds_reported` | Client-reported focus seconds (rc3-4 `_focus_seconds`, JS-wired) | Yes | int |
+| `geo_vs_claimed_property` | — (no geo-IP db) | **No** | **`"unknown"`** (never a guess) |
+| `coached_answer_score` | — (no LLM pass v1) | **No** | **`null`** (never a guess) |
+| `voice_matches_other_reference` | — (Art 9 biometric gate; v3) | **Reserved** | **ABSENT** (key never emitted) |
+| `referee_contact_invalid` | Correction-cycle second failure (AD-7, §6.4); supersedes heist-535 `referee_number_wrong` | Yes — at exhaustion | `true` / **absent** until it fires |
+
+The object stored at `result.fraud_signals` + the denormalised `reference_call.fraud_signals` column is exactly these keys (voice absent, referee_contact_invalid absent until it fires).
+
+## Scope
+
+### OWNS
+1. **`server/src/reference_checks/fraud.gleam`** (NEW) — the pure fraud-signals builder. Two entry points:
+   - `creation_fraud_signals(inputs) -> json.Json` — DB signals + line-type + honest placeholders, `form_session: null`, no `referee_contact_invalid`.
+   - `submission_fraud_signals(inputs) -> json.Json` — DB signals (re-run) + line-type (carried) + full `form_session` + placeholders.
+   - `with_referee_contact_invalid` is delivered as the SQL `stamp_referee_contact_invalid.sql` (jsonb_set on the stored column, preserving the other keys) — a DB op, not a Gleam fn. rc3-7 ships the SQL + integration tests; the RC4.3 correction-exhaustion terminal calls it.
+   Pure functions (no DB/HTTP inside); inputs passed in. Every v2-reserved signal emits its honest placeholder EXACTLY.
+2. **Phase 1 — row creation (`trigger.gleam`):** compute the pure-DB signals + run the line-type lookup (`lookup.lookup_line_type(config.twilio, config.sentry, …)`), then write the `fraud_signals` COLUMN via a new `stamp_creation_fraud_signals.sql`. `result` stays null (no result until terminal). Pre-existing rows (created before this story) keep `null` honestly.
+3. **Phase 2 — submission (`form_handler.gleam`):** capture referee IP + UA (`request_helpers.client_ip/client_user_agent`), fetch the applicant comparator (`application.submitted_ip_text`/`submitted_user_agent`) + the row's existing `fraud_signals` (to carry `line_type`) via an amended `get_form_context_by_form_token.sql`, compute `form_session`, re-run the DB signals, and write the full `fraud_signals` (embedded in `result.fraud_signals` + the column) through the existing `complete_reference_call.sql`.
+4. **Phase 3 — `referee_contact_invalid`:** the SQL stamp (`stamp_referee_contact_invalid.sql`, jsonb_set) + integration tests proving it stamps honestly + preserves the other keys (and handles a null column). The LIVE second-failure → unreachable transition is RC4.3 (does not exist today); rc3-7 provides the mechanism + never fabricates the signal.
+5. **New SQL:** `stamp_creation_fraud_signals.sql` (write the column at creation); a reuse-context read (this application's effective referee contacts + the applicant's own, for `contact_duplicate_of_applicant` + `contact_reused_within_application`); a cross-application reuse read (`contact_reused_across_applications`). Amended `get_form_context_by_form_token.sql` (+ `submitted_ip_text`, `submitted_user_agent`, `fraud_signals`).
+6. **`lookup.gleam`:** add `line_type_to_string(LineType) -> String` (fraud.gleam emits the string signal).
+7. **`result.gleam`:** `structure_form_result` takes the pre-built `fraud_signals` json (the handler builds it via `fraud.submission_fraud_signals`); the stub `form_session_fraud_signals` helper is removed (its logic moves, enriched, into `fraud.gleam`). Separation of concerns: result.gleam structures answers; fraud.gleam owns signals.
+8. **W1 cleanup (carried from rc3-6 Perkins r1):** remove the dead `claim_webhook_event` defense layer in `webhooks.gleam::apply_delivery_failure` (the discarded `case` whose every arm yields `Nil` and falls through) + correct the comments to name the real idempotency mechanism (find/mark live-status scoping). **Do NOT make it early-return** — Perkins ruled that risks at-most-once lost transitions.
+9. **Tests:** per-signal unit tests (`server/test/reference_checks/fraud_test.gleam`) incl. innocent-reuse fixtures (a letting agent across applications ≠ fraud), the weak-UA label, the honesty placeholders, the §4.2 boundary (raw IP/UA never leave the builder), and `referee_contact_invalid` stamping. Integration coverage for the Phase 1 + Phase 2 writes.
+
+### Does NOT own (deferred / sibling stories)
+- **Landlord DISPLAY** of fraud signals → RC4.1/RC4.2. rc3-7 computes + persists only.
+- **The §4.2 API stripping** (raw IP/UA out of the landlord response) → RC4.1. rc3-7 STORES `referee_ip`/`referee_user_agent` inside `form_session` (internal-only, §4.2); RC4.1 strips them at the boundary. rc3-7 touches no landlord API, so nothing leaks in this story's scope — but the keys are clearly internal.
+- **The correction FLOW + correction-exhaustion terminal** (`awaiting_correction → unreachable`) → RC4.3 (needs a timeout SLA the arch doesn't specify). rc3-7 provides `with_referee_contact_invalid`; RC4.3 calls it on exhaustion.
+- **Geo-IP, device-fingerprint library, coached-answer LLM score** → v2/v3 (AD-10 deferred; rc3-7 emits the honest placeholders only).
+- **`line_type` re-lookup on a corrected contact** → RC4.3's re-trigger. rc3-7 carries the creation-time value (avoids a paid re-lookup on every submission).
+
+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epic RC3.7 + arch AD-10/§4.2/§6.4/§9.4, FR-RC12)
+
+**AC1 — The AD-10 table, exactly + honestly**
+> **Given** the `fraud.gleam` module
+> **When** it builds signals
+> **Then** it produces exactly the table above: the three pure-DB reuse signals, `line_type`/`voip_or_burner`, and `form_session.{completion_seconds, ip_matches_applicant, device_fingerprint_match, focus_seconds_reported}`
+> **And** `geo_vs_claimed_property` is `"unknown"`, `coached_answer_score` is `null`, `voice_matches_other_reference` is **absent** (key never emitted), and `referee_contact_invalid` is **absent** until it fires — never fabricated (AD-10)
+
+**AC2 — Phase 1: creation writes DB + line-type; pre-existing rows keep nulls**
+> **Given** a new `reference_call` row is created (viewed trigger / manual start)
+> **When** creation completes
+> **Then** the `fraud_signals` column holds the pure-DB reuse signals + `line_type`/`voip_or_burner` (looked up once, before any send) + `form_session: null` + the honest placeholders, and `result` is still null
+> **And** rows created before this story (and any row whose phone has no Twilio keys) keep `null`/`unknown` honestly — never a fabricated value
+
+**AC3 — Phase 2: submission computes form_session; raw IP/UA internal-only**
+> **Given** a referee submits the form
+> **When** the submit handler runs
+> **Then** `form_session` is computed: `completion_seconds` (server `form_opened_at`→`submitted_at`), `ip_matches_applicant` (referee IP vs `application.submitted_ip_text`), `device_fingerprint_match` (referee UA vs `application.submitted_user_agent`, **labelled weak**), `focus_seconds_reported`; the DB signals are re-run; `line_type` is carried from the row's creation-time value
+> **And** the full `fraud_signals` lands in `result.fraud_signals` AND the denormalised column
+> **And** the raw referee IP/UA live only inside `form_session` (internal-only, §4.2) — only the derived booleans are the public signals
+
+**AC4 — Innocent reuse is not fraud**
+> **Given** the same letting-agent contact legitimately appears as a referee across several applications (or two slots of one application)
+> **When** the reuse signals compute
+> **Then** `contact_reused_*` is `true` (it IS reused — a clue), but the signal is a reuse clue, **never** styled as a verdict, and never auto-rejects or alters a score (AD-10, §9.4)
+
+**AC5 — `referee_contact_invalid` stamps honestly; `referee_number_wrong` superseded**
+> **Given** `fraud.with_referee_contact_invalid`
+> **When** it stamps a `fraud_signals` object
+> **Then** `referee_contact_invalid: true` is set; the slug is `referee_contact_invalid` (heist-535's `referee_number_wrong` is superseded, §6.4 — the new slug only)
+> **And** at creation + submission the signal is honestly **absent** (no correction has exhausted); the LIVE second-failure wiring is RC4.3 (the path does not exist in rc3-7's scope)
+
+**AC6 — No signal is a decision (§9.4)**
+> **Given** any fraud_signals object rc3-7 produces
+> **When** the landlord/AI consumes it
+> **Then** no signal auto-rejects an application and no signal alters an AI score; signals are display + confidence content only
+
+**AC7 — W1 cleanup: dead claim removed, idempotency intact**
+> **Given** `webhooks.gleam::apply_delivery_failure`
+> **When** the dead `claim_webhook_event` defense layer is removed
+> **Then** the comments name the real idempotency mechanism (find/mark `WHERE status IN ('queued','contact_initiated')` live-status scoping), the existing `resend_redelivery_is_idempotent_test` still passes (audit_count == 1, notification_count == 1), and the claim is NOT made early-return (Perkins: at-most-once risk)
+
+**AC8 — `make test-server` green; no em-dashes in user-facing copy**
+
+## Decisions & rationale (load-bearing — read at review)
+
+- **D1 — Creation-time `fraud_signals` persistence (write the COLUMN at creation).** §7.3 + FR-RC12 are explicit: line-type runs "at row creation, before the first message"; DB checks run "at creation and again at submission". So new rows get a creation-time `fraud_signals` (DB + line-type + placeholders; `form_session: null`). `result` stays null until terminal (§4.1); the column is the pre-submission home. "Rows created before this story keep nulls honestly" (epic AC) confirms new rows are the ones populated. *Rejected:* computing-at-creation-but-not-persisting (then why compute it; the line-type paid lookup would re-run).
+- **D2 — `referee_contact_invalid` mechanism + hook now; LIVE wiring is RC4.3.** AD-7 ties the signal to the SECOND failure (correction exhausted → `unreachable`); the `awaiting_correction → unreachable` transition does not exist yet (rc3-6 deferred it to RC4.3 — no timeout SLA in the arch). rc3-7 ships the SQL `stamp_referee_contact_invalid` (jsonb_set — operates on the stored column, not a Gleam fn), proves it with integration tests, and keeps the signal honestly absent at creation/submission. *Never fabricate a second-failure path that doesn't exist* (AD-10). The RC4.3 terminalization calls the stamp. **B1 (Perkins r1, fix applied):** the Phase-1 creation stamp is scoped to `created_ids` (the rows THIS trigger call inserted) — a wholesale re-stamp would wipe a submitted sibling's `form_session` on a supported re-trigger (`handle_start` re-fires on demand).
+- **D3 — `line_type` carried at submission (no paid re-lookup).** AD-10 scopes line-type to capture. Re-looking-up on every submission is a paid call for no v1 gain (contacts don't change until RC4.3's correction). rc3-7 carries the creation-time value from the row's existing `fraud_signals`; RC4.3's correction re-trigger re-looks-up.
+- **D4 — `completion_seconds` = server wall-clock; `focus_seconds_reported` is separate.** AD-10's row reads "Server timestamps (`form_opened_at`→`submitted_at`) + client-reported focus time" — two distinct inputs. `completion_seconds` is the server wall-clock (seconds); `focus_seconds_reported` (rc3-4) is the client-reported focus time. Both are `form_session` keys.
+- **D5 — Raw referee IP/UA stored INSIDE `form_session` (§4.2 literal), internal-only.** §4.2: "raw IPs/UAs (inside `fraud_signals.form_session`) never leave the server". So `form_session` carries `referee_ip` + `referee_user_agent` (server-side evidence) alongside the derived booleans; RC4.1 strips them at the API boundary. *Rejected alternative:* a separate internal column (diverges from §4.2; the architecture wants them inside form_session so the strip is one path).
+- **D6 — W1: remove the dead claim + fix comments (Perkins explicit).** rc3-6 Perkins r1 W1 (4-source agreement): the `claim_webhook_event` `case` is a discarded expression (Gleam has no early return) — every arm yields `Nil` and falls through to find+mark; the "Stand down" comment lies. Real idempotency = find/mark live-status scoping (`WHERE status IN ('queued','contact_initiated')`). Fix = remove the dead step + correct comments. *Not* early-return (Perkins: at-most-once lost-transition risk).
+
+## Clarify — RESOLVED (lavish, 2026-08-11; all = recommendation A)
+
+1. **D2 — `referee_contact_invalid`:** build stamping fn + hook + unit test now; **LIVE second-failure wiring is RC4.3** (the `awaiting_correction → unreachable` transition doesn't exist today — never fabricate it).
+2. **D5 — raw IP/UA:** store `referee_ip` + `referee_user_agent` **inside `form_session`** (§4.2 literal, internal-only); RC4.1 strips at the API boundary. Derived booleans are the public face.
+3. **D1 — creation-time persistence:** **write the `fraud_signals` COLUMN at creation** (DB reuse + line-type + placeholders; `form_session: null`); `result` stays null until terminal. Pre-existing rows keep null.
+4. **`device_fingerprint_match` naming:** **keep** the AD-10 name (arch-canonical). "Weak" is conveyed via a code comment + RC4 rendering — **no sibling data key** (preserves AD-10's "exactly these keys"; Perkins r1 N1).
+
